{
  "dom_id": "step-q142886",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{3}+3y)}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y\\ge 0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{3}+3y)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-3{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{3}+3y)}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\infty } \\\\  & =-3{[{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{3}+3y)}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\infty } \\\\  & =-3[0-{e}^{-(0+3y)}] \\\\  & =3{e}^{-3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3y}, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
      "choices": [
        {
          "option": "a",
          "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-142886-a",
